<div class="wrap section section--tight">
<h1>A tour of Deaftly</h1>
<p class="lede">Let's take a tour of the screens and features of the app...</p>
</div>

<div class="wrap tour">
<section id="home-screen" class="tour-step">
<img src="{{ "/screenshots/hub.webp" | asset }}" width="390" height="600" loading="lazy" alt="The Deaftly home screen, with Start typing and Use a template under Show, and Face to face and Side by side under Chat, each with an information button.">
<div>
<p class="eyebrow">The home screen</p>
<h2>Before you go</h2>
<p>Open Deaftly and everything is on one screen. Start typing or use a template when you need to say something once, clearly. Face to face and Side by side are for when it turns into a conversation. Not sure which to use? Tap the information button on any of them.</p>
</div>
</section>

<section id="face-to-face" class="tour-step">
<img src="{{ "/screenshots/face-to-face.webp" | asset }}" width="390" height="600" loading="lazy" alt="Face to face. At the top, upside down for the driver, the words Hi! I'm deaf, so I'll type. My name is Ellie Thompson. Do you need me to sign. At the bottom, the same words in the typing field.">
<div>
<p class="eyebrow">Face to face</p>
<h2>At the door</h2>
<p>Just as you're heading out, a delivery driver knocks with a parcel. They don't know you're deaf, so you start: hold your device and type “Hi! I'm deaf, so I'll type. My name is Ellie Thompson. Do you need me to sign for it?” Your words appear upside down at the top of the screen, facing them, so they read along as you type instead of waiting for you to finish. You keep a secure grip on your device the whole time.</p>
</div>
</section>

<section id="type-and-show" class="tour-step">
<img src="{{ "/screenshots/type-and-show.webp" | asset }}" width="390" height="600" loading="lazy" alt="Type and show with the message: Could I have a table for two by the window, please? A Show button sits below.">
<div>
<p class="eyebrow">Type &amp; show</p>
<h2>At the front desk</h2>
<p>At the restaurant there's a queue at the front desk. Instead of waiting to explain, you type while you wait: “Could I have a table for two by the window, please?”</p>
</div>
</section>

<section id="show" class="tour-step">
<img src="{{ "/screenshots/show.webp" | asset }}" width="390" height="600" loading="lazy" alt="The table for two message filling the screen in very large text, with a Continue as chat button below.">
<div>
<p class="eyebrow">Show</p>
<h2>Hold it up</h2>
<p>Tap Show and your message fills the screen in large, clear text the host can read from across the desk. In a dim room, switch to white on black or yellow on black. If they want to reply, tap Continue as chat.</p>
</div>
</section>


<section id="listen-for-me" class="tour-step">
<img src="{{ "/screenshots/listen.webp" | asset }}" width="390" height="600" loading="lazy" alt="Listen for me. At the top, upside down for the host, the words I'm deaf. Please speak and I'll read what you say here. Below, what the host said: Hi, welcome in. A table for two by the window? Of course. Follow me, it's just over here. A live line reads Can I get you any drinks while. A Continue side by side button sits at the bottom.">
<div>
<p class="eyebrow">Listen for me</p>
<h2>The host replies</h2>
<p>The host reads your message and starts talking. Open Listen for me: the message at the top faces them and asks them to speak, and their words appear on your screen as they talk. It all happens on your device, and the audio isn't kept. Pause whenever you like, or tap Continue side by side if you want to reply, and what they said comes with you.</p>
</div>
</section>

<section id="templates" class="tour-step">
<img src="{{ "/screenshots/fill.webp" | asset }}" width="390" height="600" loading="lazy" alt="The Order food template with Pasta arrabbiata filled in as the dish, and a Show button below.">
<div>
<p class="eyebrow">Templates</p>
<h2>Ordering</h2>
<p>At the table, open the Order food template. The parts that change are highlighted. Tap the dish and fill it in by reading the menu with your camera. Other templates let you choose from a list or type it in. Then tap Show.</p>
</div>
</section>

<section id="camera" class="tour-step">
<img src="{{ "/screenshots/camera.webp" | asset }}" width="390" height="600" loading="lazy" alt="The camera pointed at a printed Italian menu, with a box around each dish name and Pasta arrabbiata selected. An Add to message button is below.">
<div>
<p class="eyebrow">Read text with the camera</p>
<h2>Straight off the menu</h2>
<p>Point your camera at the menu and Deaftly boxes each dish it can read. Tap the one you want and add it to your message. Freeze the picture to make picking easier, and use the torch when it's dark.</p>
</div>
</section>

<section id="side-by-side" class="tour-step">
<img src="{{ "/screenshots/side-by-side.webp" | asset }}" width="390" height="600" loading="lazy" alt="Side by side chat between Me and the waiter in two colours. Me: Hi! I'm deaf. Could I have Pasta arrabbiata please? If you have a question, please type it here. The waiter asks: Sure! Do you have any allergies? Me: Yes, I'm allergic to peanuts. The waiter: Got it, thanks. I'll make sure the kitchen is aware. A switch shows it's the waiter's turn, with a microphone button beside the text box.">
<div>
<p class="eyebrow">Side by side</p>
<h2>Questions from the waiter</h2>
<p>The waiter reads your order and wants to check something, so you tap Continue as chat and pass it to them. Side by side lays the conversation out like a script, one colour each, with a clear prompt showing them where to type.</p>
<blockquote class="tour-script">
<p><strong>Me:</strong> Hi! I'm deaf. Could I have Pasta arrabbiata please? If you have a question, please type it here.</p>
<p><strong>Waiter:</strong> Sure! Do you have any allergies?</p>
<p><strong>Me:</strong> Yes, I'm allergic to peanuts.</p>
<p><strong>Waiter:</strong> Got it, thanks. I'll make sure the kitchen is aware.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Flip the switch to change turns, and swap sides to match where you're each sitting. You can add bold and highlights, quote a message, or drop in a template like Food allergy.</p>
<p>If the waiter would rather talk, they can tap the microphone on their turn and speak. Their words appear in the chat as text. It all happens on your device, and the audio isn't kept.</p>
</div>
</section>

<section id="settings" class="tour-step">
<img src="{{ "/screenshots/settings.webp" | asset }}" width="390" height="600" loading="lazy" alt="The settings screen, with First name Keisha and Last name Grant filled in, Use my first name in chats ticked, chat colours and appearance.">
<div>
<p class="eyebrow">Settings</p>
<h2>Make it yours</h2>
<p>Add your first and last name once and Deaftly fills them into templates like Check in, so you don't type your name every time. Your names stay on your device. Set your name and colour for chats, choose light, dark or system appearance, pick the colours Show starts in, and bring back any built-in templates you've deleted.</p>
</div>
</section>

</div>

